From 5d78b56f0464fa9a7813f4d10f7bf0ef9700b726 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 08:54:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 286: the ink returns as sliced RANKS and as an observer - not
 as a term in the loss

Answering a design question with the two thirds of it that survive the
measurements already on record, and refusing the third.

--ink-slices adds two edge channels to the relational graph: the RANK of the
context-fp cosine taken before the value and the rank taken after it,
separately. 277 closed fp as a search channel because it is order-blind, but
that is order-blindness INSIDE a word - arc_enc mean-pools characters. Slicing
the CONTEXT at the value is a different question and an open one, because it
recovers order BETWEEN chunks with no new machinery: two mentions that agree
on the frame but not the aftermath are a paraphrase, two that agree on both
are a duplicate, and telling those apart is exactly where the relational mind
just beat votes 0.450 to 0.000. Ranks only, never coordinates - an absolute fp
IS an identity, and identity is what turned every reading arm into a lookup
table. So the mind gets the option and decides for itself whether to weigh it.

ink_coherence is the eval-time observer: for the value the mind answered,
the mean context-fp cosine WITHIN its mentions minus the mean cosine ACROSS to
the rest. Below zero says the mentions agreeing on the value agree on nothing
else - a coalition assembled by coincidence. Reported for every arm as
when_correct against when_wrong with both denominators, and it becomes load
bearing only if those two come apart. That is the same bar the return path had
to clear in 280, and the reason it is reported beside accuracy rather than
consulted.

What is refused, and why, because the reasoning matters more than the answer:

  A term added to the loss would be a teacher through the back door. 286
  exists to remove the circularity of writing a heuristic, training the
  weights to resemble it, and scoring the resemblance - and lambda times an
  ink-disagreement penalty is that circle with an extra symbol. The tape is
  the label. If ink knowledge belongs in the mind it enters as a FEATURE the
  weights may ignore, which is what --ink-slices does.

  "Mean or trajectory over the last K slots" is two closed failure modes at
  once. A fixed window over a growing tape is failure mode 1, which cost the
  return path its measurement when top-k lost the corroborating mention; and
  collapsing a set into its mean is failure mode 8, the thing that was fixed
  by making an address a SET of member keys after 283 measured crowding at
  0.345 for the averaged key against 0.061 for two channels. The part of the
  idea worth keeping - "do these mentions point the same way" - is already in
  the graph as the pairwise cosine rank, and it is there without a window and
  without an average.

